{"translation-revision-date":"YEAR-MO-DA HO:MI+ZONE","generator":"WP-CLI\/2.12.0","source":"build\/ask-ai-promo\/index.js","domain":"messages","locale_data":{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","lang":"en","plural-forms":"nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);"},"Ask AI":[""],"Cached":[""],"An answer assistant for your visitors, built from your FAQs and the answers you write yourself.":[""],"Dashboard":[""],"Asked Questions":[""],"AI Knowledge":[""],"Settings":[""],"General":[""],"Support":[""],"How it works":[""],"Copy":[""],"Questions today":[""],"Answered for free":[""],"Last 14 days":[""],"questions per day":[""],"Today's AI budget":[""],"of %s calls":[""],"Knowledge base":[""],"Today so far":[""],"Top gaps to fill":[""],"What visitors asked in their own words. Every gap here is an answer worth writing \u2014 and once written, that question is answered for free from then on.":[""],"Questions with no answer":[""],"Answer it":[""],"Dismiss":[""],"AI":[""],"thumbs down first":[""],"More people disliked this than liked it \u2014 edit the FAQ it came from so the answer covers what they are really asking.":[""],"From your FAQs":[""],"kept in step automatically":[""],"Your own answers":[""],"Edit FAQ":[""],"Question":[""],"Do you ship to Canada?":[""],"Edit":[""],"Spending limits, abuse protection and how the answers read. Values outside the allowed range are clamped on save, so the guards can never be switched off by accident.":[""],"Cost control":[""],"These decide the most you can ever be charged in a day.":[""],"Daily AI budget":[""],"AI calls":[""],"A hard ceiling for the whole site. Cached answers and answers taken straight from a FAQ do not count against it.":[""],"Cache answers for":[""],"hours":[""],"Longer is cheaper \u2014 a repeated question then costs nothing. Set to 0 to disable caching, which is not recommended.":[""],"Answer length":[""],"words":[""],"Output is the expensive half of an AI call, so shorter answers cost less. Between 70 and 90 reads well.":[""],"characters":[""],"Budget alert e-mail":[""],"Abuse protection":[""],"Only AI calls are counted, so a visitor reading cached or FAQ answers is never locked out. Logged-in editors are never limited.":[""],"Per visitor limits":[""],"per minute":[""],"per hour":[""],"per day":[""],"The hourly limit is capped at the daily one automatically.":[""],"Minimum time before sending":[""],"seconds":[""],"Access":[""],"Only logged-in users can ask":[""],"Signed-out visitors see a \"log in to ask\" prompt instead of the form, and a floating bubble is not shown at all.":[""],"Answers":[""],"Tone":[""],"Added to the instructions the assistant follows. Leave empty for a neutral support voice.":[""],"Insights":[""],"Record unanswered questions and feedback":[""],"This is what fills the Questions section. Only the question text is stored \u2014 never the visitor.":[""],"Save changes":[""],"Limits are clamped to safe values on save.":[""],"A visitor asks a question":[""],"The block prints its form with the page, so nothing is requested and nothing is spent until somebody actually types something.":[""],"free":[""],"Bot checks":[""],"A hidden field no person can see must stay empty, the question has to be between 3 and 300 characters, and anything submitted in under two seconds is treated as a script.":[""],"Cache lookup":[""],"Questions are reduced to their meaningful words, so \"What is your refund policy?\" and \"refund policy???\" share one cached answer. A hit returns instantly and costs nothing.":[""],"An exact match answers directly":[""],"If the question is essentially one you have already answered, your wording is served as it is. No model is involved, so it is instant and free.":[""],"Limits are checked":[""],"Only now do the per visitor limits and the daily site budget apply \u2014 so somebody reading cached or FAQ answers is never locked out.":[""],"The AI writes an answer":[""],"costs a call":[""],"The journey of one question":[""],"It cannot make things up":[""],"Privacy":[""],"Upgrade to Pro":[""],"Pro dashboard":[""],"Turn your FAQs into an answer assistant":[""],"Ask AI ships with Awesome FAQ Pro, together with every other premium block and the analytics dashboard \u2014 one licence, no separate AI subscription to manage.":[""],"See it on a live site":[""],"Do you ship to Canada, and how long does it take?":[""],"Can I pay monthly instead of yearly?":[""],"Is there a discount for non-profits?":[""],"What happens to my data if I cancel?":[""],"Does the licence cover my client sites?":[""],"How long is the refund window?":[""],"You can request a full refund within 14 days of purchase \u2014 just reply to your order e-mail and we will process it, no questions asked.":[""],"Can I move my licence to another domain?":[""],"Yes. Deactivate the licence on the old site from the plugin's Activation screen, then activate it on the new one. Your remaining term carries over.":[""],"Which payment methods do you take?":[""],"All major cards and PayPal. Bank transfer is available on annual plans over five sites.":[""],"Do you offer phone support?":[""],"Support runs over e-mail and the plugin forum so every reply is written down and searchable.":[""],"From your FAQ":[""],"AI wrote it":[""],"1 call":[""],"Direct answers to visitor questions":[""],"Visitors type what they need and get instant answers based only on your FAQs. It never makes up wrong information.":[""],"See missing questions automatically":[""],"Tracks unanswered questions and ranks them by popularity, showing you exactly what new FAQs to write.":[""],"Strict daily spending limits":[""],"Set a maximum daily limit so you never spend more than planned. Get email warnings before reaching the cap.":[""],"Most answers are completely free":[""],"Saved answers and repeat questions are shown instantly without using AI credits, keeping costs very low.":[""],"Built-in protection from abuse":[""],"Automatic limits per visitor and smart bot protection stop spammers from draining your budget.":[""],"Spot unclear answers fast":[""],"Visitor ratings highlight answers with thumbs-down feedback so you can quickly improve them.":[""],"Complete visitor privacy":[""],"Only question text is saved. No names, personal details, or visitor tracking are ever collected.":[""],"Easy control over your content":[""],"Updates automatically whenever you edit your FAQs. Easily add or change custom answers anytime with zero setup.":[""],"What is your refund policy?":[""],"FAQ: Billing":[""],"How long does delivery take?":[""],"FAQ: Shipping":[""],"Do you offer student pricing?":[""],"Pricing page":[""],"added from a gap":[""],"added by hand":[""],"A question box, answered in seconds":[""],"Clickable suggested questions":[""],"Rotating hints in the empty field":[""],"Sources under every answer":[""],"AI answers labelled as AI":[""],"A \ud83d\udc4d \/ \ud83d\udc4e on each answer":[""],"A \"still need help?\" fallback link":[""],"Your colours, fonts and spacing":[""],"Questions your FAQs miss, ranked":[""],"One click from a gap to an answer":[""],"Write answers no FAQ has to carry":[""],"Extra wordings for the same answer":[""],"Answer from your FAQs, or only yours":[""],"Pause an entry without deleting it":[""],"A daily budget nothing can exceed":[""],"Per-visitor rate limits":[""],"14 days of usage at a glance":[""],"Rated answers, worst first":[""],"Your knowledge is searched":[""],"Only what you have given the assistant is searched \u2014 your published FAQs and the answers you wrote yourself \u2014 with word endings trimmed so \"service\" matches \"services\". If nothing is close enough, the visitor gets related questions instead of a made-up answer.":[""],"The model receives your matching entries and nothing else, and is told to reply only from them. Its reply is stripped down to plain paragraphs and lists before it reaches the page.":[""],"One notice a day when 80% of the budget is gone, so the bill never arrives as a surprise.":[""],"Nobody reads a page and types a question in under two seconds, so anything faster is treated as a script.":[""],"How the assistant reads, and what it remembers.":[""],"Friendly and brief, like a helpful shop assistant":[""],"Most an entry may carry":[""],"How much of a long FAQ or a hand-written answer reaches the assistant. Raise it if your answers are being cut short.":[""],"Ask AI Block":[""],"Ask AI Admin Dashboard":[""],"asked by visitors":[""],"%s%% of everything asked":[""],"AI calls used":[""],"of a %s call budget":[""],"Gaps found":[""],"FAQs worth writing next":[""],"One bar per day. The blue part is what the AI was actually asked to answer \u2014 everything below it cost nothing.":[""],"AI answered":[""],"cached or straight from a FAQ":[""],"A ceiling you set, that nothing can push past. Cached answers and answers taken straight from a FAQ are free and never counted here.":[""],"question and answer pairs":[""],"112 from your FAQs, 16 your own answers.":[""],"Assembled from your published FAQs and kept in step on its own \u2014 editing an FAQ or changing how answers read refreshes it without being asked.":[""],"from a FAQ":[""],"cached":[""],"Straight from a FAQ":[""],"Written by the AI":[""],"The more of this bar that is green or blue, the less the assistant costs you.":[""],"Turn Your FAQs & Custom Answers into an Instant AI Answers Assistant.":[""],"Ask AI puts a question box on your site and answers only from what you have given it: your published FAQs, plus any answers you write yourself on the AI Knowledge screen. Nothing else \u2014 so it cannot invent a policy you do not have. Every question it could not answer is written down for you, which quietly turns into the best content plan you will ever get: the questions your customers are actually asking.":[""],"What the Pro dashboard shows you":[""],"These are the real panels, with sample figures in place of your own. Upgrading fills them in at this very same address \u2014 there is no new screen to learn.":[""],"The panel worth the licence on its own":[""],"See the whole list":[""],"Asked most often, answered by nothing in your FAQs yet. Write one of these up and it is answered instantly and for free from then on.":[""],"Write FAQ":[""],"What you get":[""],"Key features included with your license, built to save time and keep costs low.":[""],"What happens between a visitor pressing Ask and an answer appearing \u2014 and which of those steps costs anything.":[""],"Each step can end the request. Most questions never reach the last one \u2014 which is exactly why running this is cheaper than people expect.":[""],"The model never sees your database, your pages or the open web. It receives the visitor's question plus the entries that matched it \u2014 your FAQs and your own written answers, nothing else \u2014 and is instructed to answer from those alone. When nothing matches closely enough, the visitor is shown related questions rather than a confident guess, and you get told about it on the Asked Questions page.":[""],"Visitors are counted by a one-way hash of their address, never by the address itself, and only question text is stored \u2014 no names, no addresses, no session data. The AI provider only ever receives the question and the entries of your own that matched it.":[""],"What it takes to switch on":[""],"There is no training step, no data export and nothing to upload.":[""],"Activate the Pro licence \u2014 the Ask AI screen at this same address fills in with live data.":[""],"Add an AI provider key under Settings \u203a Connectors. One key, used by every plugin that asks.":[""],"Open AI Knowledge. Your published FAQs are already listed; write in anything they do not cover yet.":[""],"Add the Ask AI block to a page and publish \u2014 the top of your FAQ page is the obvious spot.":[""],"Set a daily budget you are comfortable with. The defaults are already conservative.":[""],"Come back in a week and read the gap list. That is the part that keeps paying.":[""],"good to know":[""],"Your FAQ content stays exactly where it is. Deactivating the licence leaves every FAQ, block and shortcode working \u2014 only the assistant stops.":[""],"Live demo site":[""],"Free versus Pro, side by side":[""],"Ask us a question first":[""],"Everything the assistant is allowed to answer from. Your FAQs feed it on their own; you add an entry by hand when the wording visitors use is not in any FAQ.":[""],"Pro feature":[""],"Nothing is hidden, and nothing needs syncing":[""],"Every published FAQ becomes an entry the moment you save it \u2014 there is no import step and no training. Edit an FAQ where it lives and the assistant picks up the new wording on the next question. What you cannot do from an FAQ page is answer a question you have not written up yet, and that is what the second half of this screen is for.":[""],"Collected from every published FAQ, with a link straight to the one an entry came from.":[""],"For answers that belong nowhere else. Nothing here is published on your site \u2014 only the assistant reads it.":[""],"wordings":[""],"Why the extra wordings matter":[""],"The one thing worth knowing before you use this screen.":[""],"Matching is done on words, not meaning":[""],"\u201cCan I get my money back?\u201d and \u201cWhat is your refund policy?\u201d mean the same thing to a person and nothing to a keyword search. So every entry can carry a list of the other ways people ask it, and each one is matched against on its own while pointing at the same answer. It is the cheapest way to make the assistant feel like it understands your visitors \u2014 and it costs nothing per question, because a match this good never needs the AI at all.":[""],"Answer the questions your FAQs miss":[""],"Ask AI ships with Awesome FAQ Pro, together with every premium block and the analytics dashboard.":[""],"This is the page people renew for":[""],"Analytics tells you which of your FAQs got read. This tells you what people wanted to read and could not find \u2014 in their own words, ranked by how many asked. You are no longer guessing which FAQ to write next; the list writes itself, and every entry you clear is one less support e-mail forever.":[""],"Each row can be copied, turned straight into a new FAQ, or dismissed if it is not worth answering.":[""],"Asked":[""],"Only the text of a question is stored \u2014 never the visitor. One button clears everything collected.":[""],"Answers & feedback":[""],"What the assistant actually replied, and how visitors rated it. A row with more thumbs down than up is pointing at a FAQ whose wording is missing the real question.":[""],"Start collecting your own list":[""],"The moment the licence is active the assistant begins recording, and the first gaps usually show up the same day.":[""],"You decide the worst case before it happens":[""],"Most people hesitate over an AI feature for one reason: an unpredictable bill. So the first thing on this screen is a hard daily ceiling, and it is a real ceiling \u2014 once the day's budget is gone, no further call is made by anyone. Add caching, per-visitor limits and an alert at 80%, and the most it can cost you is a number you chose yourself.":[""],"The real Settings screen, shown read-only":[""],"Set your own ceiling":[""],"Activate the licence and these controls become yours \u2014 with the defaults above already in place, so it is safe from the first question.":[""],"Pro":[""],"On the free plan":[""],"You have the FAQ blocks and the shortcode. Ask AI, the gap report and the premium blocks come with Pro.":[""],"See the plans":[""],"Compare free and Pro":[""]}}}